Package: TICR
Type: Package
Title: Tissue-Intrinsic Coordinates for Cell and Gene Repositioning Across Tissue States
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Shuying", "Han", email = "shuying.han@icloud.com", role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Rong", "Ma", role = "aut"))
Description: Alignment-free comparison of spatial transcriptomics sections across
    conditions. Cells are represented by an anatomical layer and a normalized
    within-layer position fitted with MorphoGAM. Two analyses operate on these
    coordinates: ranking anatomical correspondences between cell populations by the
    Jensen-Shannon distance of their positional distributions, and testing
    population-relative gene displacement (the transcript-weighted position of a gene
    relative to its host population) across conditions with random-effects
    meta-analysis over sections.
